<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_FurnaceHide.xml                    PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1 · 2026-09-11
  ============================================================================
  The furnace-beast's own leather, commissioned in full by the owner
  (RUT_ruled_commissions_wave2.md §11 q8: "COMMISSION NOW — owner overrode
  wait-for-sweep"; complete brief in §12). Replaces the Leather_Heavy
  placeholder on RUT_FurnaceBeast — §8a's fifth ruled def change.

  Lives here, beside the beast that drops it
  (Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml), so RUT_FurnaceBeast's
  leatherDef is an in-mod reference and not a cross-mod one.

  🔴 STATS ARE CALIBRATED AGAINST MEASURED VANILLA, NOT GUESSED. Read this
  pass from Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_Stuff_Leather.xml:

      stat                          LeatherBase  Leather_Heavy  Leather_Thrumbo
      MarketValue                   2.1          3.3            14
      StuffPower_Armor_Sharp        0.81         1.24           2.08
      StuffPower_Insulation_Cold    16           30             34
      StuffPower_Insulation_Heat    16           14             22
      Flammability                  1            1 (inherited)  1 (inherited)

  And the §12 brief's direction, applied:

    Insulation_Cold 36  ceiling of the campaign's leathers, just past
                        thrumbofur's 34. Heat-banking is the hide's whole
                        identity. A ~6% edge, deliberately NOT a new tier.
    Insulation_Heat  8  deliberately BAD. A stove's jacket in the Pyrelands
                        sun is a mistake, and the biome that yields it
                        punishes wearing it there. This, not the cold number,
                        is what stops it being a strict thrumbofur upgrade.
    Armor_Sharp   1.66  mineral banding beats heavy fur (1.24), never rivals
                        thrumbofur (2.08).
    Flammability   0.4  the one leather that shrugs at the standing burn —
                        hide off a beast that sleeps in embers. Overrides
                        LeatherBase's 1.
    MarketValue    5.5  mid-single digits, priced for RANCH supply rather
                        than hunt scarcity: under the reversed ban 5 a tamed
                        herd breeds (§12's own "tameable-herd economy note").
                        The counterweight is the barn catching fire, not the
                        price.

  ⚠️ ECONOMY_TRADE_SWEEP_1 ratifies or reprices every number above; §12 lists
  the three specific questions it owes (the furnace-hide/thrumbofur
  insulation-prestige boundary, ranch-supply pricing, and whether
  low-flammability leather needs a campaign-wide look). Nothing here
  pre-empts that sweep.

  Colour: the sheet's grass-gold family darkened toward ash and ember
  (biome palette #2e2410 -> #e6cf7e; the fauna wears ash, ember and gold).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="LeatherBase">
    <defName>RUT_FurnaceHide</defName>
    <label>furnace hide</label>
    <description>The banded hide of a furnace-beast, mineral seams and all. It is what the animal used to store a week of deep-dayside sun in, and it has not entirely stopped: a coat of it is warm before you put it on, and stays warm in country that would kill you. In the heat it is exactly as good an idea as wearing a stove. It is also the one leather on this planet that does not particularly want to burn.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <color>(166,124,66)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>5.5</MarketValue>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
      <StuffPower_Armor_Sharp>1.66</StuffPower_Armor_Sharp>
      <StuffPower_Insulation_Cold>36</StuffPower_Insulation_Cold>
      <StuffPower_Insulation_Heat>8</StuffPower_Insulation_Heat>
    </statBases>
    <stuffProps>
      <color>(166,124,66)</color>
      <commonality>0.02</commonality>
      <statFactors>
        <MaxHitPoints>1.6</MaxHitPoints>
        <Beauty>1.8</Beauty>
      </statFactors>
    </stuffProps>
    <!-- No tradeTags: LeatherBase carries none and neither does any vanilla
         leather (checked against Items_Resource_Stuff_Leather.xml this pass).
         Leathers reach traders through the Leathers thingCategory, which is
         inherited. -->
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
